---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { adjustPurchasingPower, cpiSeries, cpiValue, latestCompleteCpiYear } from "../lib/inflation";
import { href } from "../lib/href";
import { pricesFor } from "../lib/price-index";
import { formatMoney } from "../lib/pricing";
import { loadCatalog } from "../lib/load-catalog";

const catalog = loadCatalog();
const series = cpiSeries();
const latest = latestCompleteCpiYear();
const dollar1999 = adjustPurchasingPower(1, 1999, latest);
const index1999 = cpiValue(1999);
const indexLatest = latest == null ? null : cpiValue(latest);
const verified = catalog.sets.filter((set) => pricesFor(set.id).some((price) => price.verification === "verified"));
---
<Base title="Price archive" description="Original retail, market estimates, and US purchasing power stay in separate fields.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Price archive</p>
  <h1 class="lede">Prices stay separate until they are verified</h1>
  <p class="deck">Original retail, a sealed-market estimate, a used-market estimate, and an inflation adjustment are four different ideas. This page does not merge them into one number, and it does not rank sets while coverage is empty.</p>

  <div class="stats">
    <article class="stat"><b>{verified.length}</b><span>Sets with a verified price</span></article>
    <article class="stat"><b>{series.observations.length}</b><span>Complete CPI-U years stored</span></article>
    <article class="stat"><b>{latest ?? "—"}</b><span>Latest complete index year</span></article>
  </div>

  <section class="price-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));">
    <article class="panel">
      <h2>Original retail</h2>
      <p>Unavailable</p>
      <p class="quiet">A verified MSRP needs the set number, amount, currency, market, source, observation date, and a status of verified. A sale price from a retailer is not recorded as the original price.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel">
      <h2>Sealed market estimate</h2>
      <p>Unavailable</p>
      <p class="quiet">No licensed current-market feed is connected. An estimate would be labeled as an estimate and would not be a guaranteed sale price.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel">
      <h2>Used market estimate</h2>
      <p>Unavailable</p>
      <p class="quiet">Used and sealed values are stored as different observations. Neither is shown until a dated source exists.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Rankings are withheld</h2>
    <p>Most valuable retired sets, greatest appreciation, highest original retail, and theme or year price boards need verified coverage. With {verified.length} verified set prices in the catalog, any such list would describe the gaps more than the market. No ranking is shown.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>US purchasing power</h2>
    <p>The stored index is {series.seriesName}, series {series.seriesId}, from the {series.source}. Retrieved {series.retrievedAt}. {series.method}</p>
    {latest != null && index1999 != null && indexLatest != null && dollar1999 != null ? (
      <p>One US dollar in 1999 has the purchasing power of about {formatMoney(dollar1999, "USD")} in {latest} dollars. The 1999 annual index is {index1999}. The {latest} annual index is {indexLatest}. That sentence is about the dollar. It is not a LEGO set price.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>The purchasing-power example is withheld because a required annual index is missing.</p>
    )}
    {series.partialYearsOmitted.length > 0 && (
      <p>These years were returned with fewer than twelve numeric months and are not used: {series.partialYearsOmitted.map((row) => `${row.year} (${row.months} months)`).join(", ")}. October 2025 is marked unavailable by BLS because of a lapse in appropriations. That month is not estimated.</p>
    )}
    <p>A set page will show an inflation-adjusted original price only when that set has a verified US-dollar retail amount whose year is in this series, compared with {latest ?? "a complete year"}. The result is purchasing power, not collectible appreciation. Details are in the repository note <a href="https://github.com/YegorCreative/legoArchive/blob/main/docs/pricing.md">docs/pricing.md</a>.</p>
    <p><a href={href("sets/7140-1/")}>The 1999 X-wing set page</a> still shows every price field as unavailable.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
